cavekit-gpu-rendering.md R6 / T-527. nsLayoutUtils::PaintFrame asks the root scroll frame's
DecideScrollableLayer with aAllowCreateDisplayPort, and for the root content document that set the
displayport base to the composition size at the origin, in CSS px, on every paint. So the base the
daemon sets with jihad_layout_set_displayport2 (what the card shows, at the compositor's shift, in
layout device px: patch 0059) never reached a paint: a zoomed-in card's displayport covered only
what the margins and the clamp into the scrollable rect happened to reach. With no margins (the
daemon's first paint after a zoom, what the card shows only) desktop Wikipedia at 2.33 painted 660
of the 531..861 CSS px the card showed and the rest of the view stayed white (frame dumps,
2026-10-25: the painted edge at 1536 screen px, the aligned width of a base 1116 px wide at
resolution 1). On the GPU path, once the daemon has set the root's base
(nsLayoutUtils::JihadKeepsDisplayPortBase: the frame carries the shown size), the paint keeps it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp       |  7 +++++++
 layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h         |  3 +++
 layout/generic/nsGfxScrollFrame.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 3 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp b/layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp
index fa5ee23ab3..036734c9eb 100644
--- a/layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp
+++ b/layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp
@@ -8174,6 +8174,13 @@ nsLayoutUtils::JihadOverscanFor(nsIFrame* aFrame)
   return nsMargin();
 }
 
+/* static */ bool
+nsLayoutUtils::JihadKeepsDisplayPortBase(nsIFrame* aRootScrollFrame)
+{
+  static const bool sJihadGpu = getenv("JIHAD_GPU_COMPOSITOR") != nullptr;
+  return sJihadGpu && aRootScrollFrame && aRootScrollFrame->GetProperty(JihadShownSizeProperty());
+}
+
 /* static */ nsSize
 nsLayoutUtils::CalculateCompositionSizeForFrame(nsIFrame* aFrame, bool aSubtractScrollbars)
 {
diff --git a/layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h b/layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h
index 6dc91ce361..1252a3a055 100644
--- a/layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h
+++ b/layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h
@@ -2559,6 +2559,9 @@ public:
 
   // Jihad T-505: the GPU path's overscan of the root scroll frame (top and bottom, app units)
   static nsMargin JihadOverscanFor(nsIFrame* aFrame);
+  // Jihad T-527: on the GPU path the daemon sets the root scroll frame's displayport base itself
+  // (jihad_layout_set_displayport2): true when it has, and the paint must not replace it
+  static bool JihadKeepsDisplayPortBase(nsIFrame* aRootScrollFrame);
 
  /**
   * Calculate the composition size for the root scroll frame of the root
diff --git a/layout/generic/nsGfxScrollFrame.cpp b/layout/generic/nsGfxScrollFrame.cpp
index a260199105..ca87163980 100644
--- a/layout/generic/nsGfxScrollFrame.cpp
+++ b/layout/generic/nsGfxScrollFrame.cpp
@@ -3712,7 +3712,15 @@ ScrollFrameHelper::DecideScrollableLayer(nsDisplayListBuilder* aBuilder,
         displayportBase -= mScrollPort.TopLeft();
       }
 
-      nsLayoutUtils::SetDisplayPortBase(mOuter->GetContent(), displayportBase);
+      // Jihad T-527: on the GPU path the root's base is the daemon's (what the card shows, at the
+      // compositor's shift, in layout device px: jihad_layout_set_displayport2). Replaced here on
+      // every paint (nsLayoutUtils::PaintFrame asks the root with aAllowCreateDisplayPort), it was
+      // the composition size at the origin in CSS px, and a zoomed-in card's displayport covered
+      // only what the margins and the clamp into the scrollable rect happened to reach: with no
+      // margins, desktop Wikipedia at 2.33 painted 660 of the 861 CSS px the card showed.
+      if (!(mIsRoot && nsLayoutUtils::JihadKeepsDisplayPortBase(mOuter))) {
+        nsLayoutUtils::SetDisplayPortBase(mOuter->GetContent(), displayportBase);
+      }
     }
 
     // If we don't have aAllowCreateDisplayPort == true then should have already
